{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":22577,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"c3ab46061ed32eadf01f0effeca9845f709dfe0eede5482c55f1b712a2c8167c","packTokens":7638,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":7577,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a client requests `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement `getGoogleAuthorization` according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`, constructing the Google Workspace authorization URL from deployment-configured OAuth values.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given OAuth client ID and redirect URI are configured for deployment. when A client sends `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`. then The response status is 200 and the response contains an `authorizationUrl` reflecting the configured client ID and redirect URI and a non-empty `state`.\",\n    \"Given Required Google OAuth configuration or authorization service is unavailable. when A client sends `GET /api/auth/google/authorization`. then The response status is 503 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a client submits `POST /api/auth/sign-in`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement `signIn` according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`, exchanging the authorization code with Google Workspace using deployment-configured OAuth values and accepting only eligible Folio3 Workspace identities.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid Google Workspace authorization code and matching state identify an eligible Folio3 employee. when The client sends `POST /api/auth/sign-in` with `authorizationCode` and `state`. then The response status is 200 and the response session contains `id`, `employeeId`, `employeeName`, `corporateEmail`, `role`, and `accessToken`.\",\n    \"Given OAuth values are configured and a valid authorization code is submitted. when The API exchanges the code with Google Workspace. then The request sent to Google's token endpoint contains the configured client ID, client secret, redirect URI, authorization code, and state.\",\n    \"Given The sign-in request has a missing, invalid, or mismatched state or code, an ineligible identity, or Google service is unavailable. when The client sends `POST /api/auth/sign-in`. then The response status is 400 for an invalid request, 401 for an unaccepted identity, or 503 for an unavailable service, and each error response contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/employees/me`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getMyEmployeeProfile` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid bearer session identifies an employee with a profile and registered vehicles. when The employee sends `GET /api/employees/me`. then The response status is 200 and the response profile contains the contract's required employee fields, including `id`, `employeeId`, `employeeName`, `corporateEmail`, `dedicatedParking`, `assignedFloor`, `assignedSpace`, and the employee's `vehicles` list.\",\n    \"Given The bearer token is absent or invalid, the identity lacks access, or no employee profile exists. when A client sends `GET /api/employees/me`. then The response status is 401, 403, or 404 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/dashboard`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getParkingDashboard` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid employee bearer session and available App database identify an employee. when The employee sends `GET /api/parking/dashboard`. then The response status is 200 and the response dashboard contains the contract's required fields, including `officeDate`, `timezone`, `releaseTime`, `assignedSpace`, `spaceStatus`, `availableSpaces`, `registeredVehicle`, `workingDays`, and `workingDayRule`.\",\n    \"Given The request has no valid bearer token. when A client sends `GET /api/parking/dashboard`. then The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/parking/releases/today`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `releaseTodaysSpace` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The bearer session identifies an employee with dedicated parking and the submitted `officeDate` is today in the office timezone and releasable. when The employee posts the today-release request. then The response status is 200 and the response release contains `officeDate`, `space`, `status`, `claimableAt`, and `auditEvents`, including a `Released` action.\",\n    \"Given The request is unauthenticated, the employee is not eligible to release dedicated parking, or the release conflicts with the current parking state. when A client posts to `/api/parking/releases/today`. then The response status is 401, 403, or 409 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/vehicles`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `listMyVehicles` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with registered vehicles. when The employee sends `GET /api/vehicles`. then The response status is 200 and the response `vehicles` list contains only that employee's vehicles with contract fields, including `id`, `plate`, `make`, `model`, `color`, and `active`.\",\n    \"Given The request has no valid bearer token. when A client sends `GET /api/vehicles`. then The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/vehicles`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `registerVehicle` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid employee bearer session and vehicle input with a valid plate and optional make, model, and color are supplied. when The employee posts the vehicle input to `/api/vehicles`. then The response status is 201 and the response vehicle record contains `id`, `plate`, `make`, `model`, `color`, and `active` set to true.\",\n    \"Given The vehicle input is invalid, the request is unauthenticated, or the plate conflicts with an existing record. when A client posts to `/api/vehicles`. then The response status is 400, 401, or 409 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/releases`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `listMyReleases` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with saved releases and audit events. when The employee sends `GET /api/parking/releases`. then The response status is 200 and the response `releases` list contains only that employee's releases with contract fields, including `id`, `officeDate`, `space`, `status`, `claimableAt`, and `auditEvents`.\",\n    \"Given The request has no valid bearer token. when A client sends `GET /api/parking/releases`. then The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/parking/releases`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `scheduleParkingReleases` operation for one or more dates within the next 30 calendar days according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid employee bearer session identifies a dedicated-parking holder and `officeDates` contains one or more valid dates within the next 30 calendar days. when The employee posts the schedule to `/api/parking/releases`. then The response status is 201 and the response `releases` list contains the saved dates and a `Scheduled` audit event for each release.\",\n    \"Given The schedule request is malformed, the employee is not eligible, or dates violate the contract's date rules. when A client posts to `/api/parking/releases`. then The response status is 400, 403, or 422 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `DELETE /api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `cancelParkingRelease` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The bearer session owns an unclaimed scheduled release identified by `releaseId`. when The employee deletes `/api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`. then The response status is 200, the response release status is `Cancelled`, and its `auditEvents` list includes scheduling and cancellation events.\",\n    \"Given The release does not exist, belongs to another employee, has already been claimed, or the request is unauthenticated. when A client deletes `/api/parking/releases/{releaseId}`. then The response status is 404, 403, 409, or 401 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/availability`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getParkingAvailability` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid employee bearer session exists and office capacity, release time, and current parking allocations are configured. when The employee sends `GET /api/parking/availability`. then The response status is 200 and the response contains `officeDate`, `timezone`, `availableSpaces`, `releaseTime`, and a `floors` list with `floor`, `freeSpaces`, and `totalSpaces`.\",\n    \"Given The request has no valid bearer token. when A client sends `GET /api/parking/availability`. then The response status is 401 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `POST /api/parking/claims`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `claimParkingSpace` operation, allocating a claimable temporary space using the submitted registered vehicle, according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid employee bearer session identifies an eligible employee, the selected registered vehicle belongs to that employee, and a space is claimable for `officeDate`. when The employee posts `vehicleId` and `officeDate` to `/api/parking/claims`. then The response status is 201 and the response contains allocated `floor`, `space`, `plate`, `officeDate`, `status`, `entryStatus`, `floorCapacity`, `allocationRule`, and `authorizationScope` fields.\",\n    \"Given Two eligible employees attempt to claim the last available space for the same office date concurrently. when The employees submit claims concurrently. then The responses contain exactly one status 201 and one conflict status 409, and the successful response contains one allocated space.\",\n    \"Given The request is invalid or unauthenticated, the employee is ineligible, the vehicle or date is not eligible, or no space remains available. when A client posts to `/api/parking/claims`. then The response status is 400, 401, 403, 409, or 422 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee requests `GET /api/parking/claims/today`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `getTodaysParkingClaim` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid employee bearer session identifies an employee with an active temporary allocation for today. when The employee sends `GET /api/parking/claims/today`. then The response status is 200 and the response contains the allocation's required `ParkingClaim` fields, including `floor`, `space`, `plate`, `officeDate`, and `entryStatus`.\",\n    \"Given The employee has no temporary allocation for today or the request has no valid bearer token. when A client sends `GET /api/parking/claims/today`. then The response status is 404 or 401 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values when an error response is returned.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an employee submits `DELETE /api/parking/claims/{claimId}`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the bearer-authenticated `cancelParkingClaim` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The bearer session owns an existing claim that can be cancelled. when The employee deletes `/api/parking/claims/{claimId}`. then The response status is 200 and the response contains the contract's `ParkingClaim` fields, including `id` and the cancellation outcome status.\",\n    \"Given The claim does not exist, belongs to another employee, cannot be cancelled in its current state, or the request is unauthenticated. when A client deletes `/api/parking/claims/{claimId}`. then The response status is 404, 403, 409, or 401 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/roster`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getParkingRoster` operation with documented search, assignment, pagination parameters, response schema, and status codes in `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `assignment`, `page`, and `pageSize` filters are supplied. when The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/roster`. then The response status is 200 and the response roster page contains `id`, `page`, `pages`, and an `employees` list with contract roster fields matching the supplied filters.\",\n    \"Given The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator. when A client sends `GET /api/admin/roster`. then The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/entry-checks`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getEntranceChecks` operation with documented filters, response schema, and status codes in `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `result`, and `page` filters are supplied. when The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/entry-checks`. then The response status is 200 and the response page contains `id`, `page`, `pages`, and a `checks` list with contract entry-check fields matching the supplied filters.\",\n    \"Given The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator. when A client sends `GET /api/admin/entry-checks`. then The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a client submits `POST /api/entrance/verify`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the unauthenticated `verifyEntranceDetection` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml` and record each verification outcome in App.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A car detection has a readable plate with active temporary parking authorization for the detected office date. when The client posts the detection to `/api/entrance/verify`. then The response status is 200 and the response reports the detected plate, `verificationResult` `Authorized`, `entryStatus`, and `indicatorCommand` `Green`.\",\n    \"Given The detection is a pedestrian, motorcycle, or other non-car object. when The client posts the detection to `/api/entrance/verify`. then The response status is 200 and the response has a null `plate`, `indicatorCommand` `None`, and the contract-defined non-car outcome fields.\",\n    \"Given A car has no valid authorization, its plate is unreadable, or a required entrance service is unavailable. when The client posts the detection to `/api/entrance/verify`. then The response reports a denied or unsuccessful outcome with `indicatorCommand` `None`, and the response status is 200 for processed detections or 503 for the unavailable-service outcome.\",\n    \"Given A detection has been processed, including a non-car or unsuccessful detection. when The client posts the detection and an administrator later requests matching entry checks. then A database row records the detection time, office date and time, plate where available, verification result, entry status, and detail, and the response `checks` list contains the corresponding record.\",\n    \"Given An entrance detection request is malformed. when A client posts to `/api/entrance/verify`. then The response status is 400 and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/utilization`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getWeeklyUtilizationReport` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid administrator bearer session and an omitted or valid `weekStart` date are supplied and parking activity exists for the requested week. when The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/utilization`. then The response status is 200 and the response report contains `weekStart`, `weekEnd`, `generatedAt`, `releasedSpaces`, `temporaryClaims`, `overallUtilizationPercent`, `dailyStatistics`, and `unusedParking`.\",\n    \"Given The request is unauthenticated, the caller is not an administrator, or `weekStart` is invalid. when A client sends `GET /api/admin/utilization`. then The response status is 401, 403, or 400 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/office-settings`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getOfficeParkingSettings` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid administrator bearer session exists and office parking settings are stored in App. when The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/office-settings`. then The response status is 200 and the response contains `timezone`, `releaseTime`, `schedulingWindowDays`, `reportRecipients`, `nextReportDelivery`, and `reportSchedule` matching the stored settings.\",\n    \"Given The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator. when A client sends `GET /api/admin/office-settings`. then The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator submits `PUT /api/admin/office-settings`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `updateOfficeParkingSettings` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid administrator bearer session and valid `timezone`, `releaseTime`, and non-empty `reportRecipients` are supplied. when The administrator updates `/api/admin/office-settings`. then The response status is 200 and the response contains the saved settings fields; a subsequent response from `GET /api/admin/office-settings` returns the saved values.\",\n    \"Given The update is invalid, unauthenticated, or sent by a non-administrator. when A client sends `PUT /api/admin/office-settings`. then The response status is 400, 401, or 403 as applicable, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/activity`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getParkingActivity` operation and return the activity field as specified by the d1 reading.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `eventType`, and `page` filters are supplied, and retained activity exists. when The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/activity`. then The response status is 200 and the response contains `page`, `pages`, and an `activity` list containing matching records with the contract activity fields.\",\n    \"Given The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator. when A client sends `GET /api/admin/activity`. then The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator requests `GET /api/admin/activity`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the administrator-authorized `getParkingActivity` operation and return the events field as specified by the d2 and d3 readings.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid administrator bearer session and optional `search`, `eventType`, and `page` filters are supplied, and retained activity exists. when The administrator sends `GET /api/admin/activity`. then The response status is 200 and the response contains `id`, `page`, `pages`, and an `events` list containing matching records with the contract `ParkingActivity` fields.\",\n    \"Given The request is unauthenticated or the bearer token identifies a non-administrator. when A client sends `GET /api/admin/activity`. then The response status is 401 or 403 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a client submits `POST /api/notifications/availability`, the Folio3 Parking API shall implement the unauthenticated `sendAvailabilityNotification` operation according to `contracts/openapi.yaml`, dispatching the fixed `parking-availability` template to eligible non-dedicated employees through a configured email service.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A valid availability request has a positive `availableSpaces` value and the email service accepts dispatch for eligible non-dedicated employees. when The client posts to `/api/notifications/availability`. then The response status is 202 and the response dispatch contains request `id`, status `accepted`, `recipientCount`, and template `parking-availability`; an outbound call is recorded to the configured email delivery service for eligible recipients.\",\n    \"Given The availability request is invalid or the required email service is unavailable. when A client posts to `/api/notifications/availability`. then The response status is 400 or 503 respectively, and the response error contains the contract-defined `code`, `message`, and `field` values.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API shall persist API-managed application records in the PostgreSQL database configured by `ConnectionStrings:App` and initialize its schema on startup using the existing fresh-database `EnsureCreated` behavior.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given `ConnectionStrings:App` points to a fresh PostgreSQL database. when The API starts. then A row in PostgreSQL `information_schema.tables` identifies each created application table.\",\n    \"Given A fresh App database is configured and demo seeding is disabled. when An authenticated client registers a vehicle, the API restarts against the same database, and the employee lists vehicles. then The registration response status is 201, a corresponding row exists in the configured App database, and the later response `vehicles` list contains the saved record.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When `Seed:Demo` is true, the Folio3 Parking API shall use `App.Api/SeedData.cs` to insert schema-valid sample rows into every empty application table, using contract example values where available and plausible values otherwise.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The App database schema exists, its application tables are empty, and `Seed:Demo` is true. when The API starts and invokes the public `SeedData.Run` method. then The row count is between two and five in every application table; each table has at least two schema-valid sample rows, including at least two in non-singleton tables and at least one valid row in any contract-defined singleton table, with contract examples where available such as Aisha Rahman's employee and Toyota Corolla vehicle.\",\n    \"Given An empty database has its application tables created. when A test calls the public `SeedData.Run` method directly. then Rows are present in each application table and each seeded row is schema-valid.\",\n    \"Given The App database schema exists and `Seed:Demo` is unset or false. when The API starts and initializes its database. then The row count of demo-only sample records remains zero.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API and its contract test suite shall serve documented operations and run test scenarios using explicitly arranged records, without requiring demo-seed rows.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh App database has `Seed:Demo` false and explicitly provisioned identities as needed. when The API test suite runs contract scenarios, arranging the records each scenario requires through setup or API calls. then The response statuses and returned values are determined by test-created records, the suite completes without requiring any demo-seed row, and any empty roster response has count 0.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Folio3 Parking API repository shall not add employee, administrator, or security-guard product screens; its product surfaces remain contracted HTTP operations and API documentation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API deployment is available for inspection. when A reviewer visits the root route and API documentation and inspects the served pages and product routes. then The API health response and API documentation may be displayed, but no employee, administrator, or security-guard product screen is shown.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"All operations declared by the locked OpenAPI contract are implemented with the contract's request, response, and security definitions.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}